00:00:11.382 --> 00:00:12.425
I was gonna get him too.

00:00:12.425 --> 00:00:13.676
I had him.

00:00:13.676 --> 00:00:15.553
- So whatever you do, just don't die.

00:00:17.513 --> 00:00:21.184
[Bass thumping techno beat]

00:00:23.644 --> 00:00:24.854
- Hey, guys, I'm hitting the road again.

00:00:24.854 --> 00:00:26.314
This time I'm heading to New Orleans,

00:00:26.314 --> 00:00:27.398
the home of the Pelicans,

00:00:27.398 --> 00:00:29.942
to check out Josh Hart's battlestation.

00:00:29.942 --> 00:00:31.778
My name is Doug "Censor" Martin.

00:00:31.778 --> 00:00:33.071
I'm a professional gamer

00:00:33.071 --> 00:00:35.782
and a four-time Call of Duty champion.

00:00:35.782 --> 00:00:37.200
When I'm gaming at home,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.744
this is my battlestation, where I play.

00:00:39.744 --> 00:00:41.579
I'm excited to get to Louisiana

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:43.164
to see what Hart's looks like.

00:00:44.123 --> 00:00:46.542
Josh Hart is a shooting
guard for his new team,

00:00:46.542 --> 00:00:48.419
the New Orleans Pelicans.

00:00:48.419 --> 00:00:50.088
- [Commentator:] Josh
Hart gets a good look.

00:00:50.088 --> 00:00:52.423
[Crowd yelling]

00:00:52.423 --> 00:00:54.634
- [Censor:] Off the court,
he plays World of Warcraft.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:57.136
He's also new to gaming on PC.

00:00:57.136 --> 00:00:59.138
I've been a console gamer my whole life,

00:00:59.138 --> 00:01:01.349
so I'm here in the Big Easy

00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:05.019
to get a crash course
from Hart in PC gaming

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:07.355
and get a good look at his battlestation.

00:01:07.355 --> 00:01:08.189
What's up, Josh?

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:09.107
- Ho, what up, my boy?

00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:09.941
- How are you doin', man? You good?

00:01:09.941 --> 00:01:10.566
- I'm good, man.

00:01:10.775 --> 00:01:11.609
I can't complain.

00:01:11.609 --> 00:01:12.527
- You got a nice spot, dude.

00:01:12.527 --> 00:01:13.361
- Thank you, man.

00:01:13.361 --> 00:01:14.612
Appreciate it.

00:01:17.407 --> 00:01:19.325
I had no idea if I was supposed
to close the door or not,

00:01:19.325 --> 00:01:20.618
so I just left that shit open.

00:01:20.618 --> 00:01:21.160
- [Laughing]

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.910
- I just left that shit open.

00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:28.709
- [Censor: You just moved
here two weeks ago, right?

00:01:28.709 --> 00:01:29.419
- [Josh:] Yeah.

00:01:29.419 --> 00:01:30.545
- What's your favorite
part about this place?

00:01:30.545 --> 00:01:32.046
- The campfire.

00:01:32.046 --> 00:01:34.799
I never had a campfire before,
and I've always wanted one.

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:36.175
- Oh, you got your Chelsea jersey on.

00:01:36.175 --> 00:01:37.468
You watchin' some soccer on this Sunday?

00:01:37.468 --> 00:01:38.302
- Yeah, man.

00:01:38.302 --> 00:01:39.137
So, I'm a diehard.

00:01:39.137 --> 00:01:41.013
So, I get up; I put the whole outfit on.

00:01:41.013 --> 00:01:43.349
You gonna think, like, I'm about to go—

00:01:43.349 --> 00:01:44.600
like, I'm about to go play in the match.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:45.560
- Yeah, I just gotta say, man,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.520
I've watched you since
Villanova, since day one.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.604
I wanna know more about you.

00:01:48.604 --> 00:01:49.689
I wanna see your gaming setup,

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:50.773
and I also wanna know how you game.

00:01:50.773 --> 00:01:51.607
- Let's do it.

00:01:54.402 --> 00:01:55.695
This is the setup.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.114
- Wow, man.

00:01:58.114 --> 00:01:59.115
This is sick.

00:02:03.202 --> 00:02:05.246
You got your little, like, arcade
thingy here in the corner.

00:02:05.246 --> 00:02:06.330
- [Josh:] The NBA Jam.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.291
I probably played this probably twice.

00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:09.125
I don't know what I'mma do with it,

00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:11.252
but, hey, it's just taking
up space right here.

00:02:12.211 --> 00:02:13.379
We got the good lighting.

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:16.883
We got the dual, dual 65 inches.

00:02:16.883 --> 00:02:19.469
- This guy has the Switch
with the blue and the red.

00:02:20.887 --> 00:02:22.180
Do any other players on the team

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.515
have, like, a Switch and you
guys play together or not?

00:02:24.515 --> 00:02:26.309
- Um, Tyler Ennis did my rookie year.

00:02:26.309 --> 00:02:27.768
I played with him.

00:02:27.768 --> 00:02:30.062
Ivica Zubac, Larry Nance Jr.

00:02:30.062 --> 00:02:31.856
But I actually just got a gaming laptop,

00:02:31.856 --> 00:02:34.108
so I'mma be bringing that on the road.

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:36.861
- You got everything you
need right in front of you.

00:02:36.861 --> 00:02:39.030
Can you just go in depth about
all of your favorite things

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.573
that you got goin' on right now?

00:02:42.575 --> 00:02:45.661
[Bass thumping]

00:02:47.079 --> 00:02:48.122
- I would love to.

00:02:48.122 --> 00:02:49.332
- Please, enlighten me.

00:02:50.708 --> 00:02:53.211
- So, console we hooked up to this monitor.

00:02:53.211 --> 00:02:56.297
So, I play Madden, FIFA,
whatever I play on that.

00:02:56.297 --> 00:02:58.883
And then this would be my PC monitor.

00:02:58.883 --> 00:03:00.801
My keyboard and mouse
are both from Roccat.

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.887
So, Roccat's a German brand.

00:03:02.887 --> 00:03:04.263
Turtle Beach actually bought 'em.

00:03:04.263 --> 00:03:07.016
So, obviously I'm a Turtle Beach guy, so.

00:03:07.016 --> 00:03:08.809
I think this keyboard
actually just came out.

00:03:08.809 --> 00:03:09.936
- I don't know anything about it,

00:03:09.936 --> 00:03:11.270
but I like how it looks.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:13.064
- And that's exactly why I got it.

00:03:13.064 --> 00:03:13.898
But,

00:03:13.898 --> 00:03:15.691
like, that just sounds so nice.

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:19.320
And then this PC, Turtle Beach built it.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.822
They gave it to me, and I was
very happy that they did that.

00:03:21.822 --> 00:03:23.157
It runs very smoothly.

00:03:24.492 --> 00:03:25.743
- When did video games start for you?

00:03:25.743 --> 00:03:27.328
- It started when I was young,

00:03:27.328 --> 00:03:28.162
when I was a kid.

00:03:28.162 --> 00:03:31.999
Probably like, probably
like seven, seven, eight.

00:03:31.999 --> 00:03:32.833
- What was your first game

00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:34.544
that you remember playing
when you were seven?

00:03:34.544 --> 00:03:36.921
- First Game? It was, like, Super Mario, Nintendo 64.

00:03:36.921 --> 00:03:37.797
- You talkin' about the one

00:03:37.797 --> 00:03:38.798
where he has to, like, save
Princess Peach from Bowser?

00:03:38.798 --> 00:03:40.174
- Yeah, yeah, that one, that one.

00:03:40.174 --> 00:03:41.467
- [Mario:] Ya! Yahoo!

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:42.301
Ya!

00:03:42.301 --> 00:03:43.135
Yahoo!

00:03:43.135 --> 00:03:44.053
Yahoo!

00:03:44.053 --> 00:03:45.179
- That one's, like, still—

00:03:45.179 --> 00:03:46.847
that's still, like, one of my favorite games.

00:03:46.847 --> 00:03:47.682
- Pokémon too.

00:03:47.682 --> 00:03:49.725
Like, when I was playing on
my Game Boy or whatever.

00:03:49.725 --> 00:03:50.184
- Oh, Pokémon on the Game Boys, yeah.

00:03:50.184 --> 00:03:51.060
- Game Boy Advance.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.020
- But then they came out with
the little attachment light,

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.939
so I could just be up all night

00:03:54.939 --> 00:03:55.898
when I was supposed to be sleepin',

00:03:55.898 --> 00:03:58.109
and, like, you don't have to
turn the actual light on.

00:03:58.109 --> 00:03:59.819
You could just plug the
little light in from the top

00:03:59.819 --> 00:04:00.945
and, like, bend it over the screen,

00:04:00.945 --> 00:04:02.488
and you can, like, play during that.

00:04:02.488 --> 00:04:05.575
So that's when, like, Pokémon
really took off for me.

00:04:05.575 --> 00:04:07.243
- That was the exact same
for me too, actually.

00:04:07.243 --> 00:04:08.828
That was before they had the Game Boy SP

00:04:08.828 --> 00:04:09.662
when the light was built in.

00:04:09.662 --> 00:04:10.496
- Yeah, built in, built in.

00:04:10.496 --> 00:04:12.331
- And I used to love turning the light on

00:04:12.331 --> 00:04:15.001
